## Caching

Every data-fetching function MUST use `@st.cache_data(ttl=<seconds>)`. Default TTL is {{ cache_ttl }}s; deviate only with a documented reason. Pass filter values as function arguments (not closures) so the cache key differentiates.

## SQL organization

Any SQL that feeds a UI element lives in `apps/<slug>/queries/<name>.sql` (loaded via `sql_loader.py`), with a header block: `-- Query:`, `-- Feeds:`, `-- Schemas:`, `-- Params:`. Inline SQL is only for plumbing/discovery.

Every query also carries a human-runnable **audit trail**: `apps/<slug>/sql_review/` holds a
manifest per feature and a fully-rendered, paste-runnable `.review.sql` per filter combo, so a
person can re-run each visual's SQL in Snowsight and confirm the numbers. Generated and verified
by `streamsnow sql-review` (discover | generate | check | index); the manifest is the editing
surface — `check` flags hand-edited rendered files, uncovered queries, and stale renders, and
runs in pre-commit + CI.

## Deploy source: {{ deploy_source }}

{% if deploy_source == 'stage-copy' %}
CI pushes `apps/` to a SHA-versioned internal stage (`{{ stage_database }}.{{ stage_schema }}.{{ stage_name }}/commits/<sha>/apps/<slug>/`) and runs `CREATE OR REPLACE STREAMLIT` against that path. Snowflake never reaches out to GitHub.
{% else %}
Snowflake's `GIT REPOSITORY` pulls app source on `snow git fetch`; deploy runs `CREATE STREAMLIT ... FROM '@<repo>/branches/{{ "{" }}branch}/apps/<slug>/'` (new) or the `ABORT → PULL → COMMIT → ADD LIVE VERSION FROM LAST` refresh (existing). Requires Snowflake→GitHub network reachability.
{% endif %}
STREAMLIT objects are created in `{{ app_database }}.{{ app_schema }}`. Deploy through CI on merge to `main` — never `snow streamlit deploy` locally. (Wire the deploy workflow + your Snowflake CI credentials per the deploy docs; the generated CI workflow covers lint + schema-refs today.)

## Number formatting

Every number shown to a user includes thousand separators (`format="localized"`/`"dollar"`/`"percent"` for column configs; `f"{n:,}"` / `f"${v:,.2f}"` inline).

## Conventions

- App directories: `{domain}-{function}` kebab-case under `apps/`.
- Entrypoint is `streamlit_app.py` (not configurable). `st.set_page_config(...)` first, once. Multipage via `st.navigation` + `st.Page`.
- Import branding from the local copy: `from branding import ...`. Bare imports are correct **only** for modules beside the entrypoint (`branding`, `sql_loader`) — the app root is the only `sys.path` entry that exists deployed.
- A shared helper inside a subdirectory is imported package-qualified: `from pages._header import ...`. Bare (`from _header import ...`) works under `streamlit run`, which also adds the executing page's own directory, then `ModuleNotFoundError`s on every page deployed — a local boot and a full click-through cannot catch it. No `pages/__init__.py` needed. Never name a file in `pages/` after an app-root module or a dependency.

## Production rules

- Before shipping a page that reads a new object, verify `{{ ci_role }}` can `SELECT` it (deployed apps read with its grants — "works locally" proves nothing). Prefer schema-level `FUTURE` grants so new objects are zero-touch.
- Never pass Python `None` in `params=` — the deployed driver NULL-binds the whole parameter list (local doesn't reproduce). Optional filters go through `render_sql` tokens.
- A SQL edit that "has no effect" locally needs a full preview restart — hot-reload doesn't refresh cached query results.
- Diagnosing a deployed feature problem? Verify the actual runtime first: `SHOW STREAMLITS` / `DESC STREAMLIT <fqn>` — `snowflake.yml` only declares intent.
- DDL the apps consume but this repo doesn't deploy (passthrough views, grants) goes in dated `migrations/YYYY-MM-DD-<desc>.sql` files, committed with the consuming PR; the live object is the source of truth.
- Retire an app by moving it to `retired_apps/<slug>/` (deploy scopes to `apps/**`) — never delete; `DROP STREAMLIT` is a separate deliberate manual step.
